# Exclusion patterns for evaluate_batch.py.
#
# One glob per line. Patterns match the path relative to the folder you point
# the runner at, and the bare filename, so `README.md` matches at any depth.
# A trailing slash excludes a directory and everything under it.
#
# Use this file for documents whose frontmatter would be visible to readers:
# GitHub renders frontmatter in .md files as a table. Use `skip-evaluation: true`
# frontmatter instead for pages inside a docs site, where the generator consumes
# it. See "Excluding files" in README.md.

# Repository meta files, not API documentation
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md

# Release history, not documentation under review. A changelog scored against
# an API-reference rubric is the textbook false positive; remove this line if
# you want to see that for yourself.
CHANGELOG.md

# Note: docs/ is deliberately NOT excluded. Those pages document a tool rather
# than an API, so they take some false completeness and structure hits, but
# running the evaluator against its own documentation is the honest test.

# Guideline source text, indexed by build_index.py rather than evaluated
knowledge_base/

# Saved evaluator output, not documentation under review
report_samples/

# Generated reports: the evaluator should not score its own output
ci_report.md
batch_report.md
